00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
but the amount of effort

556
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
the boy has put into

557
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
acquiring such knowledge

558
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
or skill. this brings the most hopeless

559
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
case on a footing of equal

560
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
possibility with his more

561
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
brilliant or better off brother.

562
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
wow, that's kind of interesting, isn't it?

563
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
it's not about the attainment

564
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
of a certain level or quality

565
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
of knowledge or skill,

566
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
but the amount of effort put into

567
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
acquiring the knowledge

568
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
and skill, and it's something

569
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
that boys get to do

570
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
and succeed in as

571
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
a model for the other challenges

572
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
that they're going to meet in life.

573
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Ben Powell says a boy

574
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
in whom the inferiority

575
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
complex has been born through many

576
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
failures can have his

577
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
first win or two made

578
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
easy for him

579
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
so that he is led

580
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
to intensify his efforts.

581
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
if he is a trier, no matter how clumsy

582
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
his examiner,

583
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
can accord him his badge,

584
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
and this generally inspires

585
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
the boy to go on trying

586
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
till he wins further badges

587
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,000
and becomes normally capable.

588
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
okay, so

589
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
let's think about this for a moment.

590
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Ben Powell said

591
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,000
he wanted these badges

592
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,000
to be a gateway into

593
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
the world of work in one way,

594
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,000
that he wanted them not to have

595
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,000
a certain standard of proficiency

596
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,000
and that they had other ancillary

597
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
benefits for scouts, because,

598
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
rather than having one set

599
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
standard for proficiency,

600
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
there is an instrument, a tool

601
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,000
in this badge system

602
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:28,000
that can be used to encourage

603
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,000
taking on challenges

604
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
and improving your idea

605
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,000
of yourself. the way we evaluate

606
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
how well you've done

607
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
is not, according to the other guy,

608
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
your achievement against some set standard,

609
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,000
but the effort that you've

610
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,000
put into it.

611
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Ben Powell says some are inclined to insist

612
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
that their scouts should be first rate

613
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
before they can get a badge,

614
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,000
which is very right in theory.

615
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
you do get a few scouts pretty proficient

616
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
in this way, but our object is to get

617
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
all of our scouts interested

618
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
and active at the same time.

619
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
he goes on to say:

620
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
I do not recommend the other extreme,

621
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
namely that of almost giving away

622
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
the badges on very slight knowledge

623
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
of the subjects.

624
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
it is a matter where examiners should use

625
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
their sense and discretion,

626
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
keeping the main aim in view.

627
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
use your sense and discretion

628
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
and keep the main aim in view.

629
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
how about working with each scout

630
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
on an individual basis,

631
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
tailoring the experience

632
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
so that he gets the most out of it?

633
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
keeping the main aim in view,

634
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
which is what

635
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
the development of character

636
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
goes on to talk about the danger of badge hunting,

637
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
in other words, just earning

638
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
badges for the sake of earning badges

639
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
and badge earning

640
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
right. so

641
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:46,000
the idea of scouting is not that

642
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
it's all about earning badges

643
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
and that you should be on this

644
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,000
continuous badge hunt.

645
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,000
no, it's about earning badges

646
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
as a result of the things that you do naturally

647
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,000
as a scout, while you enjoy the outdoors

648
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
with your fellow scouts.

649
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,000
it's all very simple, isn't it

650
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:04,000
okay? so that's what

651
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Baden Powell had to say

652
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,000
about why we have

653
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
merit badges.

654
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,000
what I have to say

655
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,000
here's what you can do.

656
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,000
you can choose to keep on listening to this-

657
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,000
I'm standing solidly on my soapbox

658
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
and I'm preaching about this-

659
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
or you can just skip to the closing.

660
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
you might want to just skip to the closing.

661
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
here's the problem.

662
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
there's actually little hope

663
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
of achieving

664
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,000
the aims that Baden Powell

665
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
laid out

666
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
when he started the whole thing

667
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,000
and what we have now,

668
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
which I call the merit badge

669
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,000
industrial complex.

670
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,000
the merit badge industrial complex

671
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
that we've created-

672
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,000
has three major problems.

673
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
we think the idea

674
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:52,000
of merit badges is to get as many scouts

675
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,000
merit badges in the shortest time possible.

676
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
now, nobody will tell you

677
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,000
that that's what they're trying to do,

678
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,000
but for the most part, that's how we've engineered

679
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,000
the system. everybody should get

680
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,000
as many badges as they possibly can,

681
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,000
and you should get them all the time,

682
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,000
and we should focus huge

683
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,000
blocks of the effort that we spend in the program

684
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,000
on getting merit badges.

685
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,000
from what I observed personally

686
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:16,000
and what people tell me, I think

687
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,000
that's a reasonable statement

688
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,000
and that's how we've engineered the system.

689
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:22,000
it ought to be telling that we call

690
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,000
the people who facilitate scouts

691
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,000
getting merit badges a counselor

692
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:28,000
rather than a teacher.

693
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,000
I mean, each merit badge should be

694
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,000
an individual quest,

695
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,000
not a group exercise.

696
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
each person working with a scout on a merit badge

697
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
should be counseling them,

698
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,000
helping them along the way,

699
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,000
working with them on an individual basis,

700
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,000
not teaching big groups of scouts

701
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
and not having tests and examinations

702
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,000
at the end of things

703
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:50,000
to evaluate everybody based on a mean.

704
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:52,000
no,

705
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,000
it should be very highly individualized

706
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,000
if we want to get it the way Baden Powell intended it.

707
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,000
but that's really difficult to do

708
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,000
because the requirements for merit badges

709
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,000
have proliferated

710
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,000
and they've become incredibly restrictive

711
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,000
about the ability of a counselor

712
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:08,000
to shape the experience for an individual scout.

713
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:10,000
there's really no joint

714
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:12,000
adventure in following a set of

715
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:14,000
10 or 20 requirements that are written

716
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,000
more like an engineering spec

717
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:18,000
right than a doorway

718
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
to exploring interesting subjects.

719
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,000
I mean

720
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:24,000
the way that the badges are written,

721
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
the way the requirements are written

722
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
seems like it's intentional

723
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:30,000
to take all the fun out of it.

724
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:32,000
you know,

725
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,000
I mean, it's so closely defined

726
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,000
exactly what you have to do

727
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,000
that you have to grab the merit badge book

728
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,000
and you have to look at the merit badge book

729
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:42,000
and say this is exactly what you should do-

730
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:44,000
and here's exactly the words that you should say-

731
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:46,000
to fulfill the requirement of these badges.

732
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,000
that's why I kind of look at it

733
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,000
as an assembling line,

734
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:52,000
as kind of merit badge industrial complex,

735
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:54,000
right.

736
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
the other problem is we require specific

737
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,000
badges for ranks

738
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,000
and we eliminate what Baden Powell was thinking,

739
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:02,000
and that is merely

740
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,000
intending them as an encouragement,

741
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:06,000
and we make them into a set of standards

742
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:08,000
that must be adhered to

743
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:10,000
in the purposeful attempt

744
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:12,000
to standardize the achievements

745
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:14,000
of all of our scouts.

746
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,000
why do we need that?

747
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,000
I don't think we need that.

748
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,000
I don't think that helps us achieve our aim.

749
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,000
and while I'm on the soapbox,

750
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:24,000
I'll note, as I have many times,

751
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,000
perhaps not quite so vocally:

752
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,000
the whole merit badge industrial complex

753
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:30,000
has totally ruined the summer camp

754
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:32,000
experience and I think it's been that way

755
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:34,000
for quite a long time.

756
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,000
as a past camp director and somebody who's been involved

757
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
for 20 or 30 years

758
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:40,000
in camp programs and working with counselors

759
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,000
at camp. I've worked with

760
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,000
hundreds and hundreds of staff members.

761
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,000
I've worked with thousands

762
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,000
of scouts and probably

763
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,000
tens of thousands of scouts,

764
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:52,000
and you are helpless

765
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:54,000
to try and change anything about this,

766
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
because there's one reason that scouts go to camp

767
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,000
and one reason that

768
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
scouts take them and that is to get

769
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,000
as many merit badges as possible.

770
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:04,000
and I know people will say, oh no, no, no,

771
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,000
that's not the way that we do things.

772
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,000
I'm telling you in general.

773
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
I don't think you can argue with that conclusion.

774
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,000
if there are more merit badges at camp A,

775
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:14,000
then there are. at camp B,

776
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,000
scouts are going to go to camp A.

777
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:18,000
if scouts can come home

778
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:20,000
with more merit badges at camp A,

779
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,000
then they can. at camp B,

780
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,000
scouts are going to go to camp A.

781
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:26,000
now I won't say that this is absolutely

782
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,000
everyone. of course it isn't,

783
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:30,000
because I've talked to some of you

784
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:32,000
and corresponded with some of you

785
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:34,000
who don't like this whole merit badge

786
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:36,000
summer camp thing any more than I do.

787
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:38,000
but there's tremendous pressure

788
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:40,000
on scouts. you know our hollow tradition:

789
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:42,000
we go to summer camp

790
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,000
and knock off three to five merit badges

791
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,000
and you spend all your time sitting on your butt

792
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,000
in an air-conditioned lodge somewhere,

793
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
just like you did at school all year,

794
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,000
and it just makes me absolutely

795
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:54,000
crazy. you're at

796
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:56,000
summer camp. what are all

797
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:58,000
the marvelous things that you can do here

798
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:00,000
that you can do nowhere else?

799
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:02,000
you know? certainly not sitting in a classroom

800
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:04,000
somewhere. but now I'm beginning to

801
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:06,000
rant, so I will

802
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,000
back off a little bit

803
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,000
and stop ranting. you

804
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,000
ask: do I have an answer for all this?

805
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,000
I do.

806
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,000
I found what looks to me like

807
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,000
a really good way to handle things,

808
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,000
and I only mention it here because it's

809
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:22,000
soapbox time, not because I think we should

810
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:24,000
start a movement that goes out and makes this change,

811
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:26,000
because

812
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,000
I don't think this change will ever happen,

813
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,000
because it would be a massive sea change

814
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,000
in our organization.

815
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:34,000
but I'll tell you this:

816
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:36,000
some years ago the World Organization

817
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,000
of the Scouting Movement published a document

818
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,000
called Renewed Approach to Program.

819
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,000
if you go online

820
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,000
you can probably find it.

821
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,000
it's called the RAP-

822
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Renewed Approach to Program-

823
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,000
and Scouts Ireland and Scouts Canada

824
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:52,000
and, to my understanding, Scouts Australia-

825
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:54,000
are kind of spearheading

826
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,000
program changes

827
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,000
driven by that document,

828
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
and I think that's a lot of the things that they're doing

829
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,000
are brilliant,

830
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:04,000
and I think Scouts Ireland is probably the farthest ahead

831
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:06,000
of any Scouting organization

832
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,000
in the WOSM

833
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:10,000
implementing the ideas in that RAP program,

834
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,000
and I could go on to explain it.

835
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:14,000
